    <sys:String x:Key="L_Tour_Set_Stt_Title">Speech recognition engine</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L_Tour_Set_Stt_Body">This is where it all starts — speech recognition (STT). Options: "Built-in GigaAM" — fast and offline, right on your PC; "Whisper" — more accurate, with punctuation (better on a GPU); "Local Docker" — your own container; "External server" — your own address. Built-in GigaAM is a good start.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L_Tour_Set_Speed_Title">Check the speed</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L_Tour_Set_Speed_Body">The "Measure speed" button shows how fast speech is recognized on your hardware (lower RTF is better). If the server is unreachable, it reports honestly instead of hanging.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L_Tour_Set_Accel_Title">Acceleration (CPU/GPU)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L_Tour_Set_Accel_Body">CPU works for everyone out of the box. GPU is much faster, but only with a discrete graphics card (NVIDIA/AMD); on integrated graphics, prefer CPU. This block is visible when the built-in GigaAM is selected.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L_Tour_Set_Resume_Title">Your resume</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L_Tour_Set_Resume_Body">Paste your resume here — facts, projects, numbers. The assistant takes data strictly from here and doesn't invent anything. The more detailed, the more accurate the hints during the interview.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L_Tour_Set_Engineer_Title">Engineer mode</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L_Tour_Set_Engineer_Body">Off — the main screen stays clean. Turn it on to see fine-tuning controls on the overlay: pause/chunk sliders, speech rate presets and the equalizer.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L_Tour_Set_Transcribe_Title">File transcription</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L_Tour_Set_Transcribe_Body">This opens the window for transcribing ready-made recordings (mp4, webm, etc.): transcript with timestamps, recording summary, history and export.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L_Tour_Set_Stream_Title">Answer streaming</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L_Tour_Set_Stream_Body">The AI answer is typed letter by letter as it is generated — you can see the assistant already responding. Off by default: some gateways respond noticeably slower in streaming mode.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L_Tour_Set_Karaoke_Title">Karaoke strip</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L_Tour_Set_Karaoke_Body">A teleprompter strip on top of all windows: questions and hints large and always visible. Enable it with the checkbox on this tab or the Ctrl+Shift+K hotkey; colors, font and strip position are configured here too. The "Preview" button shows the strip live.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L_Tour_Set_Save_Title">Save your changes</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L_Tour_Set_Save_Body">Changed settings — press "Save". You can always reopen this tutorial: the "Start tutorial" button at the bottom left. Next I'll show you the main window.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L_Tour_Ov_Hello_Title">This is your assistant</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L_Tour_Ov_Hello_Body">The main window is the overlay. Interlocutor lines on the left, ready AI answers on the right. The window can be dragged by the header and resized by the edges.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L_Tour_Ov_Screenshot_Title">Photo mode: hide from capture</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L_Tour_Ov_Screenshot_Body">This button hides the overlay from recording and screen sharing: you see the hints, but the other side doesn't see them on the call or in screenshots. Press again to show it back (e.g. to take a screenshot yourself). Hotkey Ctrl+Shift+C.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L_Tour_Ov_Mic_Title">Microphone on/off</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L_Tour_Ov_Mic_Body">Mutes only YOUR microphone — the interlocutor stays audible and keeps being transcribed. Full pause of all audio — hotkey Ctrl+Shift+P. A live waveform next to it shows the level.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L_Tour_Ov_Send_Title">Send now</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L_Tour_Ov_Send_Body">The lightning button sends the line to the AI immediately, without waiting for a pause. Done — good luck with the interview!</sys:String>

