    <!-- L4: karaoke (demo hints, env hook BUDDY_KARAOKE_DEMO) -->
    <sys:String x:Key="L_Kar_Demo1">Highlight your experience with WASAPI loopback and low-latency audio — that's your key differentiator.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L_Kar_Demo2">You could answer like this: the buffer keeps 10 seconds of context and sends only the interviewer's last question to the model.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L_Kar_Demo3">Mention that VAD cuts silence, so tokens aren't wasted on pauses.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L_Kar_Demo4">If asked about privacy: audio is never written to disk, the buffer lives only in memory.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L_Kar_Demo5">Short version: the overlay is click-through, never steals focus, and is invisible during screen sharing.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L_Kar_Demo6">Add a number: end-to-end latency from a spoken word to a hint is about a second and a half.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L_Kar_Demo7">Ask in return which speech-recognition stack they use now — it shows expertise.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L_Kar_Demo8">Wrap up the topic: offer a live demo right on this call.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L_Kar_PrevQ">Tell me about your experience working with asynchronous systems?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L_Kar_PrevA1">Mention message queues, retry/backoff patterns, and a concrete project with Kafka/RabbitMQ.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="L_Kar_PrevA2">A number lands well: "processing N messages/sec with at-least-once delivery".</sys:String>

